      "side": 1,
      "message": "LGTM assume the comment is adjusted.\n\n\nTo other reviewers:\n\nI think this CL seems to be safe due to the following analysis:\n\nBefore: start mIpNeighborMonitor when the IpServer is created and stop when it enter unavailable state.\n\nAfter: start mIpNeighborMonitor when IpServer entered BaseServingState and stop when IpClient exit BaseServingState.\n\nBecuase we only start serving IpV6 after `mBpfCoordinator.addIpServer(IpServer.this);` so we will start  mIpNeighborMonitor before the starting IpV6, therefore we won\u0027t lose any ND event update. We will stop ND monitoring a little bit earlier than before but when we stop, we know there is no IpServer that is serving any downstream. So we are safe to stop the ND monitoring.",
